  "title": "Destiny 2 — Sales",
  "date": "01-28",
  "text": "Title: Destiny 2 — Sales\n\nDestiny 2 sold 50,263 copies on PlayStation 4 within its first week on sale in Japan, which placed it at number one on the weekly sales charts. The weekend consisting of September 23, Destiny 2 took the number 1 spot on the UK sales chart. Destiny 2 was also the second highest-grossing console game of 2017 in North America (behind Call of Duty: WWII), and was also Activision's biggest PC release based on units sold. Digital downloads for Destiny 2 account for more than half of the total sales of the game. Despite strong unit sales, the game failed to generate the recurring revenue that Activision wanted. As a result, Activision ended its publishing deal with Bungie in 2019. 2023 saw Bungie cut 8% of their staff due to a projected revenue miss of 45%.",
